  "tagline": "A neo-Palladian beach hotel on the Platinum Coast, with three golf courses.",
  "description": "Sandy Lane is a beach hotel on the Platinum Coast of Barbados, in the parish of St. James, with 113 rooms and suites, a five-bedroom villa and three golf courses. It stands on a crescent of white coral sand about 1,000 feet long, 30 minutes by car from Grantley Adams International Airport.\n\nThe hotel first opened in 1961 on the site of an old sugar plantation, built for the former British politician Ronald Tree by the architects Happy Ward and Jimmy Walker. The mahogany trees were left standing. It was demolished and rebuilt in the same neo-Palladian style, with a white coral stone rotunda and a marble lobby framing the sea, and reopened on St. Patrick's Day in 2001. The estate grew from 380 to 830 acres with the new golf courses.\n\nThe accommodations sit in four wings. There are 26 Orchid Rooms in the gardens, 10 Ocean Rooms and 60 Luxury Ocean Rooms facing the beach, and one-bedroom Dolphin Suites with balconies over the sea. Two-bedroom Luxury Dolphin and Luxury Orchid Suites suit families, and two Orchid Penthouses have two bedrooms, a study and a whirlpool tub. At the top, The Sandy Lane Suite has four bedrooms, a terrace infinity pool and direct beach access, with a butler. The Villa has five bedrooms, a private courtyard pool and its own butler and chef.\n\nThe hotel has five restaurants and several bars. Bajan Blue, below a marble staircase, serves European, Caribbean and Asian dishes from breakfast to dinner, with a Sunday brunch. L'Acajou serves dinner, the Spa Cafe lunch, and the Monkey Club, a brasserie, was remade in a contemporary style. The Lower Terrace under the mahogany serves afternoon tea. The wine cellar holds more than 12,000 bottles, and the Monkey Bar stays open until 2:30 in the morning.\n\nThe Green Monkey, a Tom Fazio course of par 72 and 7,343 yards, is open to resort guests only. The Country Club, also by Fazio, hosted the 2006 World Golf Championships Barbados World Cup, and the Old Nine dates from 1961. The Spa at Sandy Lane covers 47,000 square feet, with a hydrotherapy pool, cold plunge pool, cryotherapy, a panoramic sauna and a 2,500 square foot gym.\n\nThe hotel suits guests who want a beach, golf and a long-established address in the Caribbean in one place.",
